WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
- Did you ever, I heard,
this could be a joke,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.770
but did you write into Playboy for advice,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.090
like career advice?

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:06.923
- Yeah.

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:08.400
- And what kind of career opportunity

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.563
was one looking for writing into Playboy?

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.070
- I was a desperate young guy.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.630
- [Kelly] Okay, okay.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.960
- Yeah, I didn't know what
to do with my musical life.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.793
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And so,

00:00:19.793 --> 00:00:21.537
I saw this thing in Playboy magazine.

00:00:21.537 --> 00:00:25.620
My stepfather, I guess,
used to buy it, and I sent.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.466
- You just outed him, I like it, yeah.

00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:30.967
- So, I sent a letter
saying, "I have an offer

00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:34.117
"to go on the road with a girl singer.

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:37.117
"I play piano and in order to do that,

00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:40.590
"I had to leave my job
at CVS as the mail boy."

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:41.423
- Which is steady work.

00:00:41.423 --> 00:00:42.600
- [Barry] Which one should I do?

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.433
- Yeah.

00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:45.210
- And they wrote me
back and they printed it

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.937
and they said, "Take the job outside

00:00:48.937 --> 00:00:51.674
"and follow your musical notes."

00:00:51.674 --> 00:00:53.203
- Oh, I love that.

00:00:53.203 --> 00:00:55.414
- And I did, I left.

00:00:55.414 --> 00:00:56.803
- You left and you did it.

00:00:56.803 --> 00:00:58.017
- I left CVS.

00:00:58.017 --> 00:01:00.582
- So, really you have Playboy
to thank for everything.

00:01:00.582 --> 00:01:01.415
- I do.

00:01:01.415 --> 00:01:02.685
I do, yeah.

00:01:02.685 --> 00:01:04.560
- So I know that you and Bette
worked together quite a bit,

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.870
so, and did she help you
promote your first album?

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:07.703
- Well, yes.

00:01:07.703 --> 00:01:10.746
She let me, I was her music
director and conductor

00:01:10.746 --> 00:01:12.093
and the arranger.

00:01:13.068 --> 00:01:14.820
And we went on the road together.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.240
And I had this first album
and I didn't wanna leave her.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.460
And so, she was very generous.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.220
She let me open her second act.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.080
So, instead of her coming out.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:25.913
- Yeah.

00:01:25.913 --> 00:01:27.000
- The piano player came out,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.330
and that was crazy.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.340
The audience didn't want
see the piano player

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.300
singing three songs.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.140
I know that.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.940
But again, they were very kind.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.770
Bette's audiences were very kind to me

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.872
and they let me do three songs,

00:01:39.872 --> 00:01:43.440
and it was the beginning
of my performing career.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.580
- Wow, I think you're right though.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.260
I do think audiences love.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.570
I have my band do that
sometimes, like come in and out.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:52.110
I think they do love seeing
artists support other artists.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.760
I think that's a big, a big thing.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.740
- Well, she was great to let me do that.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.820
- Yeah.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:01.020
- Then I actually did take
off on my own and here I am.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.647
- I know, and then she was like, "Crap,

00:02:02.647 --> 00:02:04.657
"I shouldn't have let him sing.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.210
"I lost my musical director."

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.600
- Yeah, you're right.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.850
- [Kelly] Yeah, that's amazing.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:09.720
So wait.
- She never forgave me.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.860
- But you, I love it.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.860
She's like, "Where the hell did you go?"

